<http://example.org/multimodal-ai-knowledge-graph/fashion> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fashion ontology for the multimodal AI knowledge graph sample"@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Jia, M., Shi, M., Sirotenko, M., Cui, Y., Cardie, C., Hariharan, B., Adam, H., Belongie, S.: Fashionpedia: Ontology, Segmentation, and an Attribute Localization Dataset. ECCV 2020." ;
    dcterms:creator "Amazon Web Services" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    dcterms:rights "Licensed under CC BY 4.0, not under the MIT-0 license of the rest of the repository. Derived from the Fashionpedia ontology; the Fashionpedia authors do not endorse this sample. The definitions (rdfs:comment, skos:definition) are written for this sample."@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://fashionpedia.github.io/home/index.html> ;
    rdfs:comment "Category and attribute vocabulary reused from the Fashionpedia ontology (CC BY 4.0, https://fashionpedia.github.io/home/data_license.html). Changes made for this sample: the flat catalog is expressed in OWL 2 (groups and categories as classes, attribute families as classes with attribute values as named individuals, one has<Family> object property per family), an applicability matrix is added as property domains, hasPart links garments to parts/closures/decorations, four jewelry categories that Fashionpedia does not have (earring, necklace, bracelet, ring) are added to the group of other accessories, each marked with a skos:editorialNote, a brand knowledge-graph schema (Look, Item, Statement, Article, Line, Brand) is added, and a closed vocabulary of occasions (the class Occasion, nine named individuals and the property for from Look to Occasion) is added, each term marked with a skos:editorialNote. No Fashionpedia image or annotation is included."@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.2.0" .

